<title>USA: Teen singer wins Grammy as best new artist.</title>
<headline>Teen singer wins Grammy as best new artist.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourteen-year-old country crooner LeAnn Rimes, whose hit album &quot;Blue&quot; flew to the top of both country and Top Ten charts, won a Grammy Award for best new artist on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier in an untelevised ceremony before the awards extravaganza, Rimes won a Grammy as best female country vocalist.</p>
